course: dictionary
lesson: 3192
title: Endings: stories and words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ending has more than one meaning. The ending of a story, film or song is its last part, the bit that tells you how it all finishes. «Most stories climb a story mountain: an opening, a build-up, a problem, a resolution where the problem is sorted, and an ending.» So the ending is the final step at the top.
explain: An ending is also the last letters of a word, like -ing or -ed. These endings change a word's meaning or tense, so they matter. Some endings give hints about a word too: «words ending in -eau, like un chapeau (a hat) and un manteau (a coat), are almost always masculine» in French.
explain: Ending is also the -ing form of the verb end, which means stopping or coming to an end. When you meet a word with an ending, cover the ending with your finger and look at what is left. That is often the root word, so «jumping» becomes «jump».
explain: Some endings are silent, so you do not say them. «After ils or elles (they), the verb ending -ent is silent: ils parlent (they speak) sounds like "eel PARL".» Listening for the sound is not enough on its own: check the spelling and the words around it too.
fact: An ending is the last part of a story, film or song.
fact: An ending is also the last letters of a word, such as -ing or -ed.
fact: Ending is the -ing form of end: stopping or coming to an end.
fact: A story mountain has an opening, a build-up, a problem, a resolution and an ending.
fact: Word endings can give hints: «-eau» words like «un chapeau» are almost always masculine, and «-ette» words like «une casquette» are almost always feminine.
exercise: In «Most stories climb a story mountain», what comes last? | The opening | The problem | The build-up | *The ending
exercise: Which word has the ending -ing? | happy | *jumping | cat | walked
exercise: «une casquette» (a cap) ends in -ette. In French, words with this ending are almost always which kind? | Plural | *Feminine | Masculine | Silent
test: Which is the -ing form of the verb end? | *ending | endless | ended | ends
test: How does the ending -ent sound in «ils parlent» (they speak)? | It rings out loudly | It is spelled differently | *It is silent | It sounds like a bell
exam: In «Most stories climb a story mountain», what does the word ending mean? | Stopping or coming to an end | The last letters of a word | A type of mountain | *The last part of a story
